# Copy to .env and edit. Every setting is optional: with no .env at all
# CHKT runs on port 8321, keeps its data in ./data beside this file, and
# generates its own secret key. Apply changes with: docker compose up -d
#
# Each name starts with CHKT_ on purpose. Docker Compose lets the
# environment it runs in override this file, so a plain name like
# SECRET_KEY or TZ can be silently claimed by whatever launched compose
# (some stack managers set both for themselves).

# Which release to run. Pin it to upgrade deliberately, e.g. 1.1.14.
#CHKT_VERSION=latest

# Host port. The container always listens on 8321 inside.
#CHKT_PORT=8321

# Where the database, backups and secret key live. An absolute path is
# fine. Move the old folder first if you change this, or CHKT starts
# empty while your data sits unused elsewhere.
#CHKT_DATA=./data

# Your timezone, from the tz database. Without it CHKT runs on UTC and
# reminder times won't match your phone.
#CHKT_TZ=Europe/London

# Set to 1 when reaching CHKT over plain HTTP inside a trusted network
# (a home LAN, Tailscale). Browsers refuse Secure cookies over HTTP, so
# sign-in fails without it. Leave unset once you're behind HTTPS.
#CHKT_INSECURE_COOKIES=0

# Only for the public HTTPS setup: lets you, not a passing stranger,
# create the first account. See README.
#CHKT_SETUP_TOKEN=

# Best left unset: CHKT then generates a key and keeps it with your data,
# where your backups already cover it. Set it only to carry an existing
# key to a new server without bringing its data folder along. Lose or
# change it and every stored setting stops being readable.
#CHKT_SECRET_KEY=
